  "applicability_scope": [
    "Level 1 review of the two P39 arXiv v2 Results/Overview.lean density statements and their statement-relevant definitions, reported by Peng Zhang.",
    "Theorem 3.15 achievability: the concrete patient-scope run has target-relative lower density at least one half for every exact presentation of an indexed infinite target language.",
    "Theorem B.3: for an infinite presented subset E of the target with relative lower density alpha, patient-scope on the filtered finite-intersection closure has target-relative lower density at least alpha/2.",
    "Indexed infinite language families, exact presentations, generator-first target elements, concrete patient-scope output and finite-intersection closure definitions, including their recursive project-local defining dependencies.",
    "Core ordered lower density specialized to the increasing target enumeration, including the explicit target-infinitude argument and the two operational density wrappers.",
    "Supporting proof-certificate types guard the meaning of definitions only; they are not separate human audit claims."
  ],
